From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "omni-resolve-agent[bot]"
 <omni-resolve-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:15:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(claude-native): settle a turn while a background agent
 keeps Claude busy

Claude keeps its session status file busy while a background agent is
alive and rewrites it only when the status changes. After the Stop hook
reported idle, the runner re-read the stale busy and republished running,
so the session stayed Working and every follow-up queued until Steer.

When the Stop hook lists an unfinished background agent, the Stop edge
carries the hook's time, and the status-file poller reads a busy stamped
no later than that Stop as idle until a turn starts again. The idle pane
reaper and the runner's idle shutdown still treat the busy file as live
work.

Squashed copy of upstream PR #10849.

Not upstream yet: pulled from upstream PR #10849; drop this copy once it merges.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mhavant <matthew.hoelting@avant.com>
Docs: none (fix: a Claude session stops showing Working when its turn ends; no setting)
